  "articleBody": "A spongy or soft spot on your bathroom floor is a red flag you shouldn't ignore. Usually, it's a sign of subfloor damage, often due to moisture. This can happen from a leaky toilet, a constantly overflowing tub, or even just long-term exposure to high humidity if things aren't properly sealed. When water seeps through, it can cause the wood subfloor to rot, leading to that unsettling give underfoot. It’s not just uncomfortable; it can compromise the structural integrity of your floor and even encourage mold growth. If you're noticing this, don't wait for it to get worse. You'll want to get it inspected pretty quickly. Catching it early can prevent more extensive and expensive repairs down the line. HH Remodeling LLC can take a look and figure out the best course of action.",
